+# S004 Data model: provider retry quota
+
+**Status**: Planning design, not an observed implementation.
+
+## Scope and assumption
+
+S004 requires durable, atomic quota accounting. The repository contains no application or schema files, so this model intentionally describes the minimum relational persistence contract rather than naming a database engine or an existing table. The implementation must adapt these names to the established persistence layer discovered during `/story-tasks`.
+
+## Entities
+
+### WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+One mutable quota row per workspace.
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | identifier | Primary key; identifies the workspace whose retries are limited. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | non-negative integer | Must never be negative. A reservation decrements it only when it is positive. |
+| `updated_at` | timestamp | Updated in the same transaction as every balance change. |
+
+### RetryReservation
+
+One durable accounting record for a logical reminder send attempt.
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `reservation_id` | identifier | Primary key; becomes the provider-dispatch correlation value. |
+| `workspace_id` | identifier | Foreign key/reference to `WorkspaceRetryQuota`. |
+| `attempt_id` | identifier | Logical reminder send-attempt key; unique with `workspace_id`. Repeated begin requests reuse this record. |
+| `state` | enum | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `restored`. Terminal states never transition again. |
+| `provider_callback_id` | string, nullable | First callback identifier recorded for diagnostics/deduplication; uniqueness is scoped to the provider integration if callback IDs are globally unique. |
+| `terminal_outcome` | enum, nullable | `accepted`, `failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`; required exactly when state is terminal. |
+| `created_at` | timestamp | Reservation creation time. |
+| `terminal_at` | timestamp, nullable | Set only by the winning terminal transition. |
+
+## Relationships and invariants
+
+- One `WorkspaceRetryQuota` has many `RetryReservation` records.
+- A retry reservation is created only by a successful atomic reserve operation. Its quota debit and row creation commit or roll back together.
+- `state = reserved` is the only state eligible for a provider outcome. `accepted` changes it to `finalized`; `failed`, `timed_out`, and `cancelled` change it to `restored` and return one credit in the same transaction.
+- A duplicate begin request with the same `(workspace_id, attempt_id)` returns the existing reservation without another debit.
+- A duplicate or competing terminal callback observes the already terminal reservation and performs no balance mutation. This is the exactly-once mechanism; callback delivery itself remains at-least-once.
+- The reserve transaction must use a conditional mutation equivalent to `available_retry_credits > 0` plus row-level serialization or an equivalent compare-and-swap. Check-then-decrement in application memory is invalid because concurrent attempts could overspend the quota.
+
+## State transition table
+
+| Current state | Input | Next state | Balance effect | Idempotent result |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| none | begin attempt with credit available | `reserved` | decrement once | return new reservation |
+| none | begin attempt with no credit | none | none | quota-exhausted result |
+| `reserved` | provider accepted | `finalized` | none | return finalized reservation |
+| `reserved` | provider failed, timed out, or cancelled | `restored` | increment once | return restored reservation |
+| `finalized` or `restored` | any duplicate terminal callback | unchanged | none | return existing terminal result |
+
